00:01:18.021 --> 00:01:20.668
I think this is a great
opportunity for me to clarify

00:01:20.668 --> 00:01:23.257
my point of view on automation.

00:01:23.257 --> 00:01:26.798
I don't love automation
to the point where it's

00:01:26.798 --> 00:01:30.965
replacing something that I,
one humble man's point of view,

00:01:30.965 --> 00:01:33.705
should be done by a human, AKA,

00:01:33.705 --> 00:01:36.700
I don't like the notion of an automatic DM

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:40.299
when you follow somebody
and it feels very spammy.

00:01:40.299 --> 00:01:44.385
But I love, I use
automation at Wine Library,

00:01:44.385 --> 00:01:46.800
like, when your order is
confirmed it automatically

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:49.377
e-mails you and says your
order is ready for you.

00:01:49.377 --> 00:01:52.245
I think that there's a really fine line

00:01:52.245 --> 00:01:55.205
of what one would quantify as the thing

00:01:55.205 --> 00:01:56.737
that a human should do

00:01:56.737 --> 00:01:58.177
and the thing that a computer should do.

00:01:58.177 --> 00:02:00.174
I don't like when automation automatically

00:02:00.174 --> 00:02:03.900
populates somebody's
first name into an e-mail

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:07.023
and they're trying to "trick",
and that's what I feel.

00:02:07.023 --> 00:02:10.703
You know, to me, the
intent of the automation.

00:02:10.703 --> 00:02:13.257
You know, for example,
I ask a lot of people

00:02:13.257 --> 00:02:15.776
when they sign up for my YouTube channel

00:02:15.776 --> 00:02:19.144
to e-mail me that they
did, right, the ting.

00:02:19.144 --> 00:02:20.413
You know, DRock, show them that part.

00:02:20.413 --> 00:02:21.052
(snapping fingers)

00:02:21.052 --> 00:02:22.573
Can't you just subscribe?

00:02:22.573 --> 00:02:24.802
Oh, by the way, when you do, e-mail me.

00:02:24.802 --> 00:02:26.845
Ting.

00:02:26.845 --> 00:02:28.285
(chuckles)

00:02:28.285 --> 00:02:29.922
- [DRock] Do I have to
include you saying "ting"?

00:02:29.922 --> 00:02:32.476
- Yeah, I want to keep the "ting".

00:02:32.476 --> 00:02:35.535
You know, that part, I
tell them to e-mail me

00:02:35.535 --> 00:02:37.660
and, look, I'm getting a lot of e-mails,

00:02:37.660 --> 00:02:39.552
and I don't answer everybody.

00:02:39.552 --> 00:02:41.816
One would argue that the
automated response of,

00:02:41.816 --> 00:02:43.139
"Hey! Thanks for signing up for my thing

00:02:43.139 --> 00:02:44.671
"and check out the #AskGaryVee Show

00:02:44.671 --> 00:02:46.691
"and check out, pre-order my new book,

00:02:46.691 --> 00:02:48.874
"the #AskGaryVee book
and, you know, check out."

00:02:48.874 --> 00:02:51.335
You know, one would argue
that there's a lot of

00:02:51.335 --> 00:02:55.398
conversion there but,
to me, I, as a human,

00:02:55.398 --> 00:02:58.811
I, as Gary Vaynerchuk, ask you to sign up

00:02:58.811 --> 00:03:01.052
for my newsletter and e-mail me.

00:03:01.052 --> 00:03:03.188
I don't want, when I
say e-mail me, for that

00:03:03.188 --> 00:03:06.276
to then be the computer responds to you.

00:03:06.276 --> 00:03:06.868
Right?

00:03:06.868 --> 00:03:08.853
And so what I do is when I have a moment,

00:03:08.853 --> 00:03:11.407
I try to answer a couple of
them and just say thank you.

00:03:11.407 --> 00:03:13.996
'Cause that really was
my whole intent of that.

00:03:13.996 --> 00:03:17.107
And so, I think that, I'm
a big fan of automation

00:03:17.107 --> 00:03:22.197
for a lot of things, but
what people are trying to do

00:03:22.197 --> 00:03:26.232
is scale humans and
there's a human element

00:03:26.232 --> 00:03:29.227
that matters in these equations.

00:03:29.227 --> 00:03:32.071
None of you, not a single on
of you watching this video

00:03:32.071 --> 00:03:35.310
like it when somebody
automates something that

00:03:35.310 --> 00:03:38.409
is supposed to act like
a human and it's not.

00:03:38.409 --> 00:03:40.627
So, as a company, I
think automation's great.

00:03:40.627 --> 00:03:42.589
When you apply for VaynerMedia,

00:03:42.589 --> 00:03:44.446
I don't even know if this
happens with the resume,

00:03:44.446 --> 00:03:46.129
